UPDATE companies SET description='Unverferth Manufacturing Co., Inc. was founded in 1948 in Kalida, Ohio, by father-and-son duo Lawrence G. and Richard Unverferth. The pair started L.G. Unverferth Manufacturing with a loan backed by family war bonds, initially producing combine shucker control levers and soon after introducing bolt-on dual-wheel extensions for tractors. The company incorporated as Unverferth Mfg. Co., Inc. The business has remained family-owned and operated throughout its history.

The company manufactures a broad line of agricultural equipment across four production sites in Kalida and Delphos, Ohio; Shell Rock, Iowa; and a fourth location. Core processes include precision machining, welding, fabrication, powder coating, and final assembly, supported by in-house product design and engineering. The product portfolio spans grain carts and wagons, header transports, seed tenders, fertilizer applicators, tillage tools, augers and conveyors, and agricultural dual, replacement, and specialty wheel systems. These products are sold under six brands — Blu-Jet, Brent, Orthman, Parker, Top Air, and Unverferth — through eight sales and distribution branches in the United States and Canada.

The company also supplies replacement and dual-wheel systems for tractors and combines.

Unverferth states its mission is to help the farming community become more efficient through innovation and quality manufacturing. The company emphasizes its patent portfolio — covering dual-wheel mounting systems, grain cart unloading augers, seed tender conveyors, and sprayer section-control technology — as a differentiator, along with the ability to control design, fabrication, and coating under one roof at its Kalida headquarters.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision machining", "Welding", "Fabrication", "Powder coating", "Assembly", "Product design and engineering", "Manufacturing of grain carts and wagons", "Manufacturing of header transports", "Manufacturing of seed tenders", "Manufacturing of fertilizer application equipment", "Manufacturing of tillage equipment", "Manufacturing of augers and conveyors", "Manufacturing of agricultural dual and replacement wheel systems", "Manufacturing of anhydrous ammonia applicators", "Manufacturing of liquid fertilizer applicators", "Manufacturing of sprayers", "Manufacturing of strip-till tools", "Manufacturing of soil conditioners", "Manufacturing of running gears", "Manufacturing of conveyor systems"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Grain handling", "Fertilizer application", "Tillage", "Spraying", "Seed handling", "Agricultural wheel systems"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["T-Tank sprayer", "Air Command\u2122 Section Control System", "Seed Runner bulk tender", "X-Series grain carts", "Brent Avalanche grain cart", "Rolling Harrow soil conditioner", "Culti-Planter tillage tool", "Turn-Rite running gears", "Circoloc dual wheel system", "Ultra-Torque direct-axle duals"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1948", "Four manufacturing locations and eight sales/distribution branches across the U.S. and Canada", "Six integrated brands (Blu-Jet, Brent, Orthman, Parker, Top Air, Unverferth) covering grain handling, fertilizer application, tillage, seeding, and wheel systems", "In-house precision machining, welding, fabrication, powder coating, and assembly at the Kalida headquarters", "Extensive patent portfolio on dual-wheel systems, grain carts, seed tenders, and sprayer technology"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1948 in Kalida, Ohio by Lawrence G. and Richard Unverferth -> /about-us", "Family-owned and operated -> / (Our Company section)", "Four manufacturing locations and eight sales/distribution branches across US and Canada -> / (Our Company section)", "Six brands: Blu-Jet, Brent, Orthman, Parker, Top Air, Unverferth -> / (Our Brands section)", "Processes: precision machining, welding, fabrication, powder coating, assembly, product design and engineering -> / (Kalida facility description)", "Products: grain carts, wagons, header transports, seed tenders, fertilizer applicators, tillage tools, augers, conveyors, wheel systems -> / (Our Company section)", "Industries served: grain handling, fertilizer application, tillage, spraying, seed handling -> / (Our Brands and industries_served)", "Patent portfolio mentioned throughout history -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Kalida, OH -> / (Kalida facility description)", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Unverferth Manufacturing Co., Inc. is a family-owned and operated agricultural equipment manufacturer producing a wide range of products that help the farming community be more efficient.", "founded_year": "1948", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/unverferth-manufacturing-co.-inc./"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='unverferth-manufacturing-co-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Urschel Laboratories was founded in 1910 in Valparaiso, Indiana, by William E. Urschel, who invented the Gooseberry Snipper. The company, now headquartered in Chesterton, Indiana, became 100% employee-owned through an ESOP on March 3, 2016, with Patrick Urschel serving as CEO.

The company designs and builds industrial food cutting machines — dicers, slicers, shredders, and milling equipment — capable of slicing, dicing, strip cutting, shredding, granulating, milling, and pureeing a wide range of products from fruits and vegetables to meat, cheese, and pet food. Its product line includes models such as the Little Gem Aspire Dicer, M VersaPro Dicer, DiversaCut series, Sprint series, Affinity series, and Model M6. Urschel serves customers in over 130 countries and has operated across four generations.

Its equipment is used by food processors worldwide for applications such as slicing potatoes, dicing tomatoes, shredding lettuce and cheese, pureeing nut milks and vegetables, milling nut butters, and processing meat and poultry. The machines serve the broader food processing industry, including fruit, vegetable, potato, meat, cheese, baked goods, and pet food segments.

The company traces its competitive edge to its founding principle — a machine that could do the work of 100 workers in a day — and continues to invest in patented cutting technology through its Innovation & Development team. The employee-ownership model is cited as a driver of long-term commitment and product reliability.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Industrial food cutting machine manufacturing", "Precision slicing", "Precision dicing", "Strip cutting", "Shredding", "Granulating", "Milling", "Pureeing", "Comitrol processing", "Research and development of cutting technology"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Fruit and vegetable processing", "Potato processing", "Meat processing", "Cheese processing", "Baked goods", "Pet food processing", "Commercial food processing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Little Gem Aspire\u2122 Dicer", "M VersaPro\u00ae Dicer", "DiversaCut 2110A\u00ae Dicer", "Sprint 2\u00ae Dicer", "DiversaCut Sprint\u00ae Dicer", "Affinity\u00ae Dicer", "Affinity Integra\u00ae Dicer", "Affinity\u00ae Integra-D Dicer", "Affinity\u00ae CD-L Dicer", "Model M6 Dicer"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% employee-owned (ESOP) since 2016", "Patented Urschel cutting technology", "Innovation & Development team driving R&D", "Presence in 130+ countries", "Four generations of continuous operation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1910 in Valparaiso, Indiana by William E. Urschel -> /", "Headquarters Chesterton, Indiana -> db", "100% employee-owned ESOP since March 3, 2016 -> /", "Patrick Urschel CEO -> /", "130+ countries worldwide -> /", "4 generations -> /", "110+ years in business -> /", "Manufactures industrial food cutting machines (dicers, slicers, shredders, milling equipment) -> /", "Product models: Little Gem Aspire Dicer, M VersaPro Dicer, DiversaCut 2110A, Sprint 2, DiversaCut Sprint, Affinity Dicer, Affinity Integra, Affinity Integra-D, Affinity CD-L, Model M6 -> /", "Industries: food processing, fruit/vegetable, potato, meat, cheese, baked goods, pet food -> /", "Applications: slice potatoes, dice tomatoes, shred lettuce, puree nut milks, mill nut butters, process meat/poultry -> /", "Patented technology, Innovation & Development team -> /", "KRONEN partnership expansion into Asia and Italy -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We continue to lead the world in the manufacturing and selling of industrial cutting equipment to the food processing and allied industries.", "founded_year": "1910", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='urschel-laboratories-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company does not disclose its founding year or ownership structure in its public materials.

The shop provides custom steel fabrication, engineering, installation, and field services. Its certified welders work in MIG, TIG, and flux‑core processes, while CNC plasma cutting is handled on a Burn Table and an Inovatech 600 Beamline powered by Hypertherm. A dedicated blast‑and‑paint booth supports sand, soda, and hydro blasting plus epoxy, urethane, Irathane, and Duromar coatings. The detailing department produces BIM and CAD models using Tekla, Advanced Steel, and AutoCAD, drawing on over 50 years of combined senior‑designer experience.

Utah Fabrication serves municipalities, mining, energy, and transportation sectors across the western United States and has shipped work internationally. Its painting and coating crew focuses on power plants, mining, heavy industrial, and marine applications, while Tekko targets mining, power, and oil‑and‑gas markets.

The company emphasizes integrity, accountability, and respect, stating it "inspects what it expects." Differentiators cited include AISC, ASME, and AWS‑certified welders; a NACE‑certified coatings engineer and HAZMAT technician on staff; all personnel MSHA and confined‑space trained; and a turnkey approach from design through field erection.', certifications=ARRAY['ASME Stamps','AISC certified','AWS certified welders','NACE Certified Coatings Engineer']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural steel fabrication", "MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Flux\u2011core welding", "CNC plasma cutting", "Burn table cutting", "Inovatech 600 Beamline cutting", "Sandblasting", "Soda blasting", "Hydro blasting", "Epoxy coating", "Urethane coating", "Irathane coating", "Duromar coating", "BIM detailing", "CAD detailing", "Tekla modeling", "Advanced Steel modeling", "AutoCAD drafting", "Field installation", "Heavy industrial construction", "Turnkey project management"], "industries": ["Municipalities", "Mining", "Energy", "Transportation", "Power generation", "Heavy industrial", "Marine", "Oil and gas"], "materials": ["Structural steel", "Epoxy coatings", "Urethane coatings", "Irathane coatings", "Duromar coatings"], "equipment": ["Burn Table", "Inovatech 600 Beamline powered by Hypertherm", "Blast and paint booth facility"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["AISC, ASME, and AWS\u2011certified welders", "NACE\u2011certified coatings engineer and HAZMAT technician", "All staff MSHA and confined\u2011space trained", "In\u2011house blast and paint booth with sand, soda, and hydro blasting", "Turnkey projects via Tekko installation arm"], "facts_used": ["Location: Tooele, UT -> db (hq_city, hq_state_label) and page ''/'' (address)", "Founded on principle of best product at reasonable price -> page ''/''", "Services: fabrication, engineering, installation, field services -> page ''/''", "Welding processes: MIG, TIG, flux core -> page ''/''", "Cutting equi