UPDATE companies SET description='Uzelac Industries was founded in 2003 by Michael Uzelac in Greendale, Wisconsin, after he acquired Poja Sheetmetal (established 1956) and later Duske Engineering (established 1980). The family-owned company began as a contract fabrication shop and evolved into a specialist in direct-fired rotary dryer design and manufacturing.

The company engineers and builds custom direct-fired rotary drying systems, delivered factory-assembled for minimal on-site installation. It also provides turnkey fabrication services for large equipment OEMs, with capabilities that include brake bending, rolling, shearing, punching, MIG and TIG welding, and waterjet cutting. The plant houses a 25-ton crane bay and a 10-ton crane bay, each with 22.5 feet of clear hook height. The workforce consists of journeymen fabricators and engineers with over 40 years of experience in dryer design, and the firm holds several U.S. patents.

Uzelac serves the hemp, poultry, biomass, rendering, biosolids, and gasification industries. In poultry, it has supplied rotary drying systems to Herbruck’s Poultry Ranch, Michael Foods, Foster Farms, and Tyson for more than 30 years. Its drying systems are installed worldwide.

The business traces its roots to the craftsmanship of Poja Sheetmetal and the engineering of Duske Engineering, carrying forward core values of integrity, customer satisfaction, and innovation. Michael Uzelac launched the venture to combine those legacies into a single design-build manufacturer of rotary drying equipment.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom direct-fired rotary dryer design and manufacturing", "Turnkey equipment fabrication", "Large equipment OEM fabrication services", "Brake bending and rolling", "Shearing and punching", "MIG and TIG welding", "Waterjet cutting", "Stainless steel fabrication", "Aluminum fabrication", "HR/CR steel fabrication", "Low quantity complex fabrication", "Factory-assembled dryer installation"], "industries": ["Hemp", "Poultry", "Biomass", "Rendering", "Biosolids", "Gasification"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Hot rolled steel", "Cold rolled steel"], "equipment": ["25-ton crane bay (22.5 ft clear under hook)", "10-ton crane bay (22.5 ft clear under hook)", "Waterjet cutting system", "Brake bending and rolling equipment", "Shearing and punching equipment", "MIG and TIG welding equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom direct-fired rotary dryers designed per customer specifications", "Factory-assembled dryers requiring minimal on-site installation", "Over 40 years of combined rotary dryer manufacturing heritage", "Several U.S. patents in dryer design", "In-house fabrication with 25-ton and 10-ton crane bays"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2003 by Michael Uzelac after acquiring Poja Sheetmetal (1956) and Duske Engineering (1980) -> db", "Family-owned, relocated to Pewaukee, Wisconsin in 2024 -> /", "17,100 sq ft facility with 25-ton and 10-ton crane bays -> /about", "Custom direct-fired rotary dryer design and manufacturing -> /", "Fabrication services: brake bending, rolling, shearing, punching, MIG/TIG welding, waterjet cutting -> /about", "Journeymen fabricators and engineers with 40+ years experience -> /about", "Several U.S. patents in dryer design -> /about", "Industries served: hemp, poultry, biomass, rendering, biosolids, gasification -> /", "Poultry clients: Herbruck\u2019s Poultry Ranch, Michael Foods, Foster Farms, Tyson -> /", "Global installation base -> /about", "Core values: integrity, customer satisfaction, innovation -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Uzelac Industries specializes in engineering, design, and manufacturing custom direct-fired rotary drying systems. In addition to the core dryer business, they also provide fabrication services for large equipment OEMs.", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='uzelac-industries-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='VESCO-NM is based in Albuquerque, New Mexico. The company was founded in 2009 by Dr. Abdel-Rahman EL-Emawy, who earned his Ph.D. from Colorado State University in 1996 with a dissertation on the growth of II/VI materials by MBE. After a career as an aircraft avionics engineer and a research professor at the University of New Mexico’s Center for High Technology Materials, Dr. El-Emawy established VESCO-NM to commercialize his expertise in MBE and MOCVD equipment.

The company designs and manufactures proprietary Molecular Beam Epitaxy (MBE) systems—including the Ultima 310 model—and components such as valved crackers, effusion cells, RF plasma sources, and heaters. It also produces components for Metal Organic Chemical Vapor Deposition (MOCVD) systems. Beyond new equipment, VESCO-NM provides decommissioning, decontamination, installation, and refurbishment services for semiconductor cleanroom tools worldwide. Its Albuquerque facility houses a machine shop with CNC milling, CNC lathe, wire EDM, water jet, and welding stations, plus a clean room for assembly and testing and CAD workstations for design and simulation.

VESCO-NM serves research facilities, universities, private industry, and government agencies across the globe, with over 300 customers served. Its equipment supports applications in semiconductor crystal growth, LED manufacturing, renewable energy, thin-film technologies, and consumer electronics. The company has worked with most existing MBE and MOCVD system platforms.

Dr. El-Emawy founded the business to deliver smart designs and the highest quality products at reasonable prices, backed by world‑class customer service and a commitment to meeting deadlines. The company emphasizes unique equipment designs that enable innovation in materials growth and deposition.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Molecular Beam Epitaxy (MBE) systems manufacturing", "MBE components manufacturing", "MOCVD components manufacturing", "Semiconductor cleanroom tools decommissioning", "Decontamination and cleaning services", "Installation of MBE & MOCVD systems", "Refurbishment of MBE & MOCVD systems and components", "Valved crackers manufacturing", "Effusion cells manufacturing", "RF plasma sources manufacturing", "MBE heaters manufacturing", "CNC milling", "CNC lathe", "Wire EDM", "Water jet cutting", "Welding", "Clean room assembly and testing", "CAD design and simulation"], "industries": ["Semiconductor", "Research facilities", "Universities", "Private industry", "Government", "LED manufacturing", "Renewable energy", "Thin-film technologies", "Consumer electronics"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["CNC milling", "CNC lathe", "Wire EDM", "Water jet", "Welding stations", "Clean room", "CAD software design workstations"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary MBE system designs (e.g., Ultima 310)", "Comprehensive decontamination and cleaning services for semiconductor tools", "Global service footprint with 300+ customers served", "In-house machine shop with CNC, EDM, water jet, and welding capabilities", "Clean room assembly and testing facility"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2009 by Dr. Abdel-Rahman EL-Emawy -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Albuquerque, New Mexico -> /about-us, db", "Manufactures proprietary MBE systems (Ultima 310) and components -> /, /about-us", "Produces MOCVD components -> /, /about-us", "Provides decommissioning, decontamination, installation, refurbishment services -> /, /about-us", "Facility includes machine shop with CNC milling, CNC lathe, wire EDM, water jet, welding stations -> /about-us", "Facility includes clean room for assembly and testing -> /about-us", "Uses CAD software design workstations -> /about-us", "Serves research facilities, universities, private industry, government worldwide -> /about-us", "Over 300 customers served worldwide -> /", "Core values: Quality, Value, Service, Delivery -> /about-us", "Dr. El-Emawy background: aircraft avionics engineer, Ph.D. 1996, research professor at UNM CHTM -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "VESCO-NM manufactures state of the art proprietary Molecular Beam Epitaxy (MBE) systems and components", "founded_year": "2009", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vesco-nm' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Victor Wire & Cable was founded in 1954 in Los Angeles, California. For decades the company operated as a landmark in the city before relocating to a new facility in 2017. The business has remained focused on custom wire and cable manufacturing since its inception.

The company designs and manufactures custom wire and cable products, including multi-conductor, composite, and coaxial constructions. Its capabilities cover mil-spec, low-noise, UL-listed, and RG174 coaxial cables, as well as specialized cables for oil and gas, nuclear, robotics, travel, heater, and battery applications. Victor Wire & Cable also provides engineering assistance to develop custom sensor cables, outdoor data cables, and harsh-environment cables, supported by a full range of wire and cable manufacturing equipment.

Victor Wire & Cable serves customers in oil and gas, nuclear, robotics, and a broad range of industrial sectors. Its cables are used in applications such as sensor systems, data communications, and harsh-environment installations. The company works with clients who require custom cable solutions for unique or demanding requirements.

Victor Wire & Cable emphasizes its more than 50 years of experience and its status as a UL-certified manufacturer. The company highlights its engineering support and ability to deliver custom cable solutions that meet exacting specifications, including mil-spec standards.', certifications=ARRAY['MIL SPEC','UL certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom wire manufacturing", "Custom cable manufacturing", "Mil-spec cable manufacturing", "Low-noise cable manufacturing", "UL-listed cable manufacturing", "RG174 coaxial cable manufacturing", "Multi-conductor composite cable manufacturing", "Oil and gas cable manufacturing", "Nuclear cable manufacturing", "Robotics cable manufacturing", "Travel cable manufacturing", "Heater cable manufacturing", "Battery cable manufacturing", "Sensor cable manufacturing", "Outdoor data cable manufacturing", "Harsh environment cable manufacturing", "Engineering assistance for custom cable design"], "industries": ["Oil and gas", "Nuclear", "Robotics", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 50 years of custom wire and cable manufacturing experience", "UL-certified custom wire and cable manufacturer", "Specializes in unique multi-conductor, composite, and coaxial cables", "Provides engineering assistance for custom cable solutions", "MIL SPEC certified"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1954 -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Los Angeles, California -> db", "Relocated to new facility in 2017 -> /about-us", "UL-certified custom wire and cable manufacturer -> /", "MIL SPEC certification -> db", "Specializes in multi-conductor, composite, and coaxial cables -> /about-us", "Over 50 years of experience -> /about-us", "Provides engineering assistance for custom cable solutions -> /about-us", "Manufactures cables for oil and gas, nuclear, and robotics applications -> /", "Produces custom sensor cables, outdoor data cables, and harsh environment cables -> /", "Offers full range of wire and cable manufacturing equipment -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Victor Wire & Cable is a Custom Wire & Cable manufacturer specializing in unique Multi-Conductor, Composite and Coaxial Cables.", "founded_year": "1954", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='victor-wire-cable' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='VRG Components, Inc. was founded in 2014 in Matthews, North Carolina, as an independent worldwide distributor of electronic components. The company was established with the mission of supplying electronics manufacturers with high-quality components to maximize their production processes.

The firm operates as a global sourcing partner for new, allocated, end-of-life, last-time-buy, and long-lead-time electronic components, semiconductors, and network components from over 500 manufacturers across more than 50 product lines. Its AS9120-certified quality processes support a catalog of over 50,000 available parts, backed by a multi-lingual sourcing team and exclusive access to global inventory.

VRG serves automotive tier 1–3 suppliers, electronic manufacturing services providers, and contract manufacturers, as well as medical device makers, transportation systems builders, machinery manufacturers, telecommunications firms, and consumer electronics producers. Customers turn to the company when primary suppliers cannot deliver shortage or obsolete parts.

The company distinguishes itself through AS9120 certification, a commitment to quote turnaround within 30 minutes, and a focus on solving supply-chain gaps that other distributors cannot fill. Its founders designed the business to be unlike typical suppliers, emphasizing speed, quality standards, and long-term relationships with customers and vendors worldwide.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9120']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Global sourcing of electronic components", "Authorized distribution for select manufacturers", "Shortage and obsolete component sourcing", "End-of-life and last-time-buy procurement", "Long lead-time component mitigation", "Quick quote turnaround (30 minutes)", "Supply chain gap fulfillment"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Medical Electronics", "Telecommunications", "Transportation", "Machinery", "Consumer Electronics"], "materials": ["Electronic components", "Semiconductors", "Network components"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["AS9120 certified quality processes", "Quotes turned around in 30 minutes or less", "Multi-lingual sourcing team (German, Spanish)", "Access to exclusive global inventory from 500+ manufacturers", "Specializes in shortage, allocated, end-of-life, and long-lead-time components"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2014 -> db", "Headquarters Matthews, North Carolina -> db", "AS9120 certified -> /", "Independent worldwide distributor of electronic components, semiconductors, network components -> /", "Global sourcing for new, allocated, end-of-life, LTB, long lead time components -> /", "500+ manufacturers, 50+ product lines, 50,000+ parts available -> /", "Multi-lingual team (German, Spanish) -> /", "Quick quotes within 30 minutes -> /", "Industries: Automotive, Medical Electronics, Transportation, Machinery, Telecommunications, Consumer Electronics -> /", "Authorized distributor for wenglor sensoric, Lutronic, Lumberg -> /", "Named Supply Chain Connect Top 50 Electronics Distributor 2024 -> /", "Inc. 5000 honoree 2023 -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "VRG Components\u00ae is an industry-leading, AS9120 certified, independent worldwide distributor of electronic components, semiconductors, and network components from hundreds of product manufacturers.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": ["German", "Spanish"], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vrg-components-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Valley Services Electronics (VSE), headquartered in San Jose, California, with a second facility in Reno, Nevada, has been realizing electronic designs for over 40 years. The company operates as a U.S.-based contract manufacturer serving design teams and supply chain departments across the technology sector.

VSE provides end-to-end electronics manufacturing services, including PCBA design and engineering, printed circuit board assembly (from prototype through high-volume production), box build assembly, wire harness and cable assembly, and comprehensive testing such as in-circuit, functional, environmental, HIPOT, and X-ray inspection. The San Jose facility focuses on new product introduction (NPI) and quick-turn prototyping, while the Reno site handles larger production runs. The company emphasizes high-mix, low- to mid-volume builds with design-for-manufacturing and design-for-test support, backed by strategic sourcing and component authenticity controls.

The company serves industries including aerospace, biotechnology, telecommunications, semiconductor, medical devices, clean technology, automotive, renewable energy, and industrial equipment. Customers range from entrepreneurial teams launching first products to established firms requiring domestic manufacturing with regulatory compliance.

VSE’s stated differentiation rests on five pillars: scalable production with a boutique approach, supply chain resilience through domestic assembly and verified components, speed to market via streamlined handoffs and direct communication, secure transparent partnerships protecting intellectual property, and total quality compliance with IPC and ISO standards at every stage. The firm’s mission is to empower life-changing technologies worldwide by uniting engineering, design, assembly, and testing in a single streamlined process.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485','ITAR','RoHS','IPC 610']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCBA design and engineering", "PCB assembly (prototype, low-volume, high-volume)", "Box build assembly", "Wire harness and cable assembly", "In-circuit testing", "Functional testing", "Environmental testing", "HIPOT testing", "X-ray inspection", "Supply chain management and strategic sourcing", "Component procurement and authenticity verification", "DFM/DFT support", "NPI (new product introduction) manufacturing", "Turnkey assembly", "Multilayer PCB fabrication", "Rigid-flex PCB fabrication", "HDI PCB fabrication", "High-speed PCB design", "Custom electronic enclosures", "RoHS compliant manufacturing"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Biotechnology", "Telecommunications", "Semiconductor", "Medical Devices", "Clean Technology", "Automotive", "Renewable Energy", "Industrial Equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production (high-mix, low- to mid-volume)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Dual facilities: San Jose for NPI and quick-turn prototyping, Reno for high-volume production", "High-mix, low- to mid-volume manufacturing with DFM/DFT support", "Vertically integrated supply chain with domestic assembly and verified components", "ISO 9001 and ISO 13485 registered, ITAR compliant, RoHS compliant", "In-house testing: in-circuit, functional, environmental, HIPOT, and X-ray"], "facts