UPDATE companies SET description='Vermont Steel Erection and Fabrication is based in Wolcott, Vermont. The company traces its roots to 1998 when Gerard Bellavance founded United Steel Erectors. The business remains family-owned; Bellavance''s sons Gabriel, Eliott, and Addison have since joined the leadership team, and the name was later changed to Vermont Steel Erection and Fabrication.

The company provides steel erection, steel fabrication, and welding services across New England. Its shop handles MIG, TIG, and stick welding, and crews can also travel to job sites for mobile welding. Work ranges from structural steel installation to custom fabrication of items such as vehicle frames, heavy-equipment components, dumpsters, and storage racks.

The company cites projects involving vehicles, heavy equipment, dumpsters, and racks as typical examples of its welding and fabrication work.

