UPDATE companies SET description='Vital Plastics, LLC was founded in 1994 in Baldwin, Wisconsin, where it operates two manufacturing facilities east of the Twin Cities metro area along Interstate 94. The company is a custom plastic injection molding and assembly solutions provider.

A cellular manufacturing model and RJG scientific molding practices underpin production, supported by IQMS integration for real-time process data. Beyond molding, Vital Plastics offers a full suite of assembly services—automated, semi-automated, and hand-set—including heat staking, ultrasonic welding, hot stamping, pad printing, and kitting. Tooling maintenance, design, modifications, and warehousing round out the operation. The firm reports a 99.86% on-time delivery rate and has shipped more than 700 million assembled components with a 0.004% defect rate.

Vital Plastics serves Fortune 1000 companies and applies engineering expertise across multiple industries, supporting projects from prototype through high-volume production. Its capabilities include insert molding, overmolding, two-shot molding, and processing of engineered, commodity, filled, unfilled, and high-temperature exotic resins.

The company’s stated mission is to make the “Vital Difference” by centering customers, community, and employees. Its vision emphasizes innovation, sustainable practices, and empowering teams, while core values highlight integrity, respect, teamwork, customer focus, persistence, and innovation. Vital Plastics also positions itself as a domestic reshoring alternative to offshore production.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding (30\u2013400 ton)", "Insert molding", "Overmolding", "Two-shot molding", "Automated assembly", "Semi-automated assembly", "Hand-set assembly", "Heat staking", "Ultrasonic welding", "Hot stamping", "Pad printing", "Kitting", "Tool maintenance", "Tool design", "Tool modifications", "Tool warehousing", "Design for manufacturing (DFM)", "Mold-flow analysis", "PPAP (Levels 1\u20135)", "Gauge R&R studies", "Initial Sample Inspection Reports (ISIR)", "CMM inspection", "Optical comparator inspection", "Lot traceability"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Engineered grade resins", "Commodity grade resins", "Filled resins", "Unfilled resins", "High-temperature exotic resins"], "equipment": ["56 injection molding presses (30\u2013400 ton)", "5-axis robots", "Sprue pickers", "Environmental controls", "Coordinate measuring machine (CMM)", "Optical comparator", "Custom fixtures", "Gauges, micrometers, calipers"], "volume": "Prototype to full-scale production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Cellular manufacturing model for consistent quality", "RJG scientific molding practices for optimized performance", "IQMS integration providing real-time production metrics", "99.86% on-time delivery rate", "Over 700 million assembled components shipped with 0.004% defect rate"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1994 -> /about", "Two manufacturing locations in Baldwin, WI -> /about", "Over 50 30-400T injection molding machines -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /about", "100+ dedicated emplo