UPDATE companies SET description='Walker Woodworking operates from a 75,000-square-foot facility in Shelby, North Carolina. The company was incorporated in 2000 by Travis Walker, a former paramedic who began woodworking as a hobby in the 1990s. After borrowing $3,000 from his grandmother for tools in 1996, he worked from his aunt’s garage and his father-in-law’s shop before opening a 2,100-square-foot plant. His wife, Stacey, joined as a full-time partner in 2006, and the business remains family-owned.

The shop produces custom and semi-custom cabinetry for kitchens, bathrooms, entertainment centers, and built-ins, along with cabinet lighting routing and extrusion preparation for aluminum extrusions. In-house engineers, artisans, and craftsmen — 32 strong as of the latest update — handle design, machining, assembly, and installation of lighting components. The facility replaced a 10,000-square-foot building in 2021, following six earlier expansions.

Walker Woodworking serves homeowners, interior designers, and builders across the region. Its showroom, Greenbrook Design Center, opened in 2018 in downtown Shelby, provides a space for clients to review materials and designs. The company had completed over 400 kitchen projects by 2012 and continues to serve both residential and light commercial projects.

The founders’ original passion — turning a grandfather’s red oak into heirloom pieces — still drives the operation. The company emphasizes locally handcrafted work, a no-cookie-cutter approach, and community-focused values. Strategic growth, including the 2021 facility relocation, was pursued to maintain personalized service and quick adaptation to client needs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinet manufacturing", "Semi-custom cabinet manufacturing", "Cabinet lighting routing and extrusion preparation", "Aluminum extrusion machining", "Installation and testing of lighting components", "Service and repair", "Appliance panel replacement", "Design and engineering", "CNC routing"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Interior design", "Kitchen and bath remodeling", "Commercial cabinetry", "Builder/Contractor services"], "materials": ["Wood", "Aluminum extrusions"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Locally handcrafted in Shelby, NC by a team that lives and works in Cleveland County", "Custom and semi-custom cabinetry with no cookie-cutter solutions", "In-house production enabling quick adaptation to changes", "Family-run leadership fostering a team fueled by passion and service", "75,000 sq ft facility housing engineers, artisans, and craftsmen under one roof"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2000 -> /about", "Family-owned -> /about", "75,000 sq ft facility -> /about", "32 employees -> /about", "Custom and semi-custom cabinetry -> /about", "Aluminum extrusion routing -> capabilities", "Installation and testing of lighting components -> products", "Service and repair -> capabilities", "Appliance panel replacement -> capabilities", "Greenbrook Design Center showroom -> /about", "Over 400 kitchen projects by 2012 -> /about", "Travis Walker founder -> /about", "Stacey Walker partner -> /about", "Shelby, NC location -> /about", "Homeowners, designers, builders as customers -> /", "Sustainability practices -> /", "Tours available -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Walker Woodworking has been providing high-quality, locally manufactured custom cabinetry.", "founded_year": "2000", "employee_count": "32", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='walker-woodworking-manufacturing-plant' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
