UPDATE companies SET description='Wapsie Valley Creamery, a family-owned dairy processor, has operated in Independence, Iowa since 1906.

The company manufactures cheese, lactose, and whey products at its Independence processing plant, sourcing raw milk from over 170 independent dairy farms across eastern Iowa, southwestern Wisconsin, and northwestern Illinois. A workforce of approximately 140 employees runs the facility, which has continuously updated its manufacturing processes and equipment to handle larger milk volumes and improve product yields.

Cheese is sold to large wholesale companies that cut and shred it into private-label packages for retail distribution. Lactose goes to food manufacturers for use in confectionery, sweeteners, and dairy blends. Reduced-lactose whey is supplied to wholesalers for processed cheese, cheese spreads, and calf milk replacer.

Wapsie Valley Creamery states that its point of difference is a commitment to surpass normal quality standards. The plant operates under inspection by the USDA, FDA, and state agencies, maintains an on-site quality assurance laboratory, and uses outside labs for pathogen testing, while ongoing equipment upgrades aim to boost processing efficiency.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cheese manufacturing", "Lactose production", "Whey processing", "Milk reception and testing", "Quality assurance and laboratory testing"], "industries": ["Dairy processing", "Food manufacturing", "Confectionery", "Animal feed", "Wholesale distribution"], "materials": ["Raw milk"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned operation since 1906", "Milk sourced from over 170 independent dairy farms", "Inspected by USDA, FDA, and state agencies", "On-site quality assurance laboratory with outside lab verification", "Ongoing equipment upgrades to increase processing efficiency"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1906 -> /about-us", "Family-owned -> /about-us", "Headquarters Independence, Iowa -> /about-us", "140 employees -> /about-us", "Manufactures cheese, lactose, whey -> /about-us", "Milk from 170+ independent farms -> /about-us", "Sells cheese to wholesale cutters/shredders for private label -> /about-us", "Lactose sold to food manufacturers for confectionery, sweeteners, dairy blends -> /about-us", "Whey sold to wholesalers for processed cheese, spreads, calf milk replacer -> /about-us", "Continuous equipment investment for higher yields -> /about-us", "Operates under USDA, FDA, Iowa Dept of Agriculture, Iowa Public Health Dept inspections -> /quality", "On-site QA laboratory and outside lab testing -> /quality", "Commitment to surpass normal quality standards -> /quality"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Wapsie Valley Creamery, Inc. (Wapsie) is a family-owned business which manufactures cheese, lactose, and whey products at its Independence, Iowa processing plant.", "founded_year": "1906", "employee_count": "140", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wapsie-valley-creamery' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ward''s Manufacturing operates from Warren, Rhode Island, where siblings Kiffin and Kelly Ward founded the company in 2022. The brother‑sister team, both former buyers of fabrication services, launched the shop after experiencing the difficulties of sourcing reliable domestic metalwork. Their family background includes a grandfather who was a carpenter rebuilding post‑war London and another who worked as an auto mechanic and metalworker, instilling a service‑oriented trade ethic. The business is certified as a woman‑owned small business.

The shop provides fiber laser cutting (3 kW, 5 × 10 ft bed, ±0.001″ cut tolerance), CNC press brake bending (190‑ton, up to 10 ft length), machining (thread cutting, countersinking, counterboring, reaming, inserts, laser etching), and in‑house finishing (#4 brushed, vibratory tumbling, glass bead blasting, orbital sanding). Product design and engineering support covers CAD creation from sketches, design optimization, and GD&T expertise. Value‑added services include powder coating, wet painting, anodizing, assembly, welding, and a range of surface treatments. There is no minimum order quantity; the company runs from single prototypes to production runs of tens of thousands of units and has shipped to 43 U.S. states and four Canadian provinces.

Customers span aerospace and defense, marine and boat building, robotics and automation, electronics and enclosure fabrication, renewable energy (wind turbine and solar components), medical devices, industrial equipment, automotive, and niche sectors such as shellfish aquaculture, art, and custom signage. The client base consists mainly of small‑to‑mid‑sized OEMs and manufacturers across North America who require tight tolerances and fast turnaround.

