UPDATE companies SET description='Western Energy Systems, operating as Northeast-Western Energy Systems USA, LLC (NES-WES), is headquartered in Brea, California. The company traces its roots to 1964 and was acquired by the INNIO Group in 2023, bringing additional resources to its power generation and microgrid businesses. With over 50 years of experience in reciprocating engine power applications, NES-WES has evolved into a full-service integrator of combined heat and power (CHP) and distributed generation (DG) solutions.

NES-WES designs, engineers, and maintains CHP and DG systems ranging from 50 kW to 22 MW, with a focus on gaseous fuels including natural gas, biogas, propane, and syngas. The firm provides end-to-end integration of balance-of-plant components such as heat recovery, fuel gas handling, emissions control, cooling systems, switchgear, transformers, and power plant controls. Its engineering team performs electrical system studies, protective relaying, and relay coordination, while field project managers oversee installation, pre-commissioning, startup, and acceptance testing. The company employs between 200 and 499 people.

The company serves utility, industrial, commercial, institutional, and governmental customers. Notable projects include the Bergen County Wastewater Treatment plant, Covidien''s New Haven CHP installation, Mount Joy Wire, landfill-gas-to-energy facilities, High Sierra California Cogeneration, and Techni-Cast industrial cogeneration. Clients typically seek to reduce energy costs, improve resilience, and lower carbon footprints.

NES-WES emphasizes a balance of innovative solutions and time-tested approaches, aiming to exceed customer expectations. The 2023 acquisition by INNIO Jenbacher strengthened its position in the power generation and microgrid markets, allowing it to offer fully integrated, climate-neutral energy solutions from a single source.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CHP system integration", "DG system integration", "Switchgear integration", "Fuel gas compressor system integration", "Battery storage integration", "Microgrid system integration", "Heat recovery system engineering", "Emissions control system integration", "Cooling system integration", "Electrical system studies", "Protective relaying and coordination", "Field project management", "Installation and commissioning", "Black start system engineering", "Dual-fuel system engineering", "Absorption chiller integration", "Biogas cleaning system integration", "Cooling tower integration", "Transformer integration", "Power plant control system integration"], "industries": ["Energy", "Utilities", "Industrial", "Commercial", "Institutional", "Governmental", "Wastewater treatment", "Healthcare", "Manufacturing", "Landfill gas-to-energy"], "materials": ["Natural gas", "Biogas", "Propane", "Syngas"], "equipment": ["Jenbacher CHP and DG systems", "Fuel gas compressors", "Mechanical chillers", "Absorption chillers", "Biogas cleaning systems", "Cooling towers", "Switchgear", "Transformers", "Power plant control systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 50 years of reciprocating engine power application experience", "Fully integrated CHP and DG solutions up to 10 MW power blocks", "Fuel flexibility across natural gas, biogas, propane, syngas, and automated dual-fuel setups", "End-to-end balance-of-plant integration including heat recovery, emissions, and controls", "Field project management and commissioning support for installation and startup"], "facts_used": ["Head