UPDATE companies SET description='Western Washington Sheet Metal JATC operates as a non-profit union training center headquartered in Everett, Washington, with a second campus in DuPont. The joint apprenticeship committee traces its roots to a sheet metal apprenticeship tradition spanning over 100 years, with the modern program structure in place since 1973. It is governed by a committee of six labor trustees from SMART Local 66 and six management trustees from SMACNA Western Washington.

The JATC runs a five-year sheet metal apprenticeship combining on-the-job training with classroom instruction across four disciplines: general sheet metal fabrication and installation, testing adjusting and balancing (TAB), HVAC service, and residential sheet metal. At any given time roughly 500 apprentices are enrolled, and the program graduates approximately 98 journey-level workers each year. Instruction is delivered by seven full-time instructors supported by three administrators and two support staff, collectively holding nearly 210 years of industry experience.

The DuPont campus hosts the SMART Heroes program, providing a direct entry route for active-duty military personnel and veterans. The program also partners with Bates Technical College for associate-degree credit.

The committee’s stated mission is to bring labor and management together to develop a highly skilled, competitive workforce for the evolving sheet metal industry. By offering tuition-free training, zero student debt, and a clear path to union wages and benefits — including retirement, family medical, dental, and vision — the JATC positions the apprenticeship as a career alternative to traditional college pathways.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sheet metal fabrication and installation training", "Testing, adjusting, and balancing (TAB) training", "HVAC service training", "Residential sheet metal training", "Welding instruction (SMAW, FCAW)", "Commissioning training", "Controls and building automation training", "Energy auditing training", "Smoke control and fire/life safety training", "Blueprint reading and layout", "Bluebeam software training", "Mechanical systems troubleshooting"], "industries": ["Sheet metal construction", "HVAC", "Commercial construction", "Healthcare construction", "Data center construction", "Institutional construction", "Testing adjusting balancing (TAB)", "Architectural sheet metal", "Residential sheet metal"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Tuition-free apprenticeship with no student debt", "Direct pathway to union journey-level wages and benefits", "SMART Heroes program for military veterans and active-duty personnel", "72 signatory contractors hiring graduates", "Over 100 years of apprenticeship tradition"], "facts_used": ["Headquartered in Everett, WA with campus in DuPont, WA -> /about", "Non-profit union training center (JATC) -> /about", "Apprenticeship tradition over 100 years, modern program since 1973 -> /about", "Governed by 6 labor trustees (SMART Local 66) and 6 management trustees (SMACNA Western Washington) -> /about", "Five-year apprenticeship across four disciplines: sheet metal, TAB, HVAC service, residential -> /about", "~500 a