UPDATE companies SET description='Westshore Electronics was founded in 2003 in Holland, Michigan. The company began as an engineering-focused operation providing electronic and mechanical design alongside software development, aiming to help customers move from concept to production.

Today the firm operates as a single-source electronics manufacturer, offering double-sided surface-mount assembly, flexible and metal-core PCB assembly, through-hole and mixed-technology builds, automated selective wave soldering, microcontroller programming, and full functional testing. Its equipment handles fine-pitch placement down to 01005 packages and ball-grid-array components, and it provides conformal coating, cable assemblies, and finished-goods box builds. The shop supports IPC Class 2 and 3 work and runs PPAP-capable processes.

Westshore serves small and mid-tier manufacturers in the medical, industrial-controls, durable-goods, and inspection-lighting sectors. Customers typically need embedded control systems, high-density circuit boards, LED PCBAs, instrument lighting, and electromechanical controls, and the company manages component sourcing and supply-chain logistics alongside design and production.

The company emphasizes a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015, reinforced by on-site IPC training, a proprietary Track-Trace-Control system, and risk-mitigation tools such as PFMEA, PPAP, first-article inspection, and 8D problem solving. Its stated differentiation is the ability to act as a full-lifecycle electronics partner from ideation through volume production.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fine pitch component placement (0402, capability to 01005)", "BGA (ball grid array) placement", "Conformal coating", "IPC Class 2 and 3 inspection", "PPAP (Production Part Approval Process)", "Double-sided surface mount assembly", "Flexible printed circuit board assembly", "Metal core printed circuit board assembly", "Through-hole and mixed technology assembly", "Automated selective wave soldering", "Microcontroller programming", "100% functional testing", "Component wiring", "Finished goods assembly (box build)", "Electronic and mechanical design", "Software/firmware development", "Cable assembly", "LED PCBA assembly", "Instrument lighting assembly", "Electromechanical controls assembly", "Component sourcing and supply chain management"], "industries": ["Medical", "Industrial Controls", "Durable Goods", "Inspection Lighting"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-source design through production", "IPC Class 2/3 and PPAP capabilities", "Fine-pitch placement capability to 01005", "ISO 9001:2015 certified QMS with on-site IPC training", "Proprietary Track, Trace, and Control (TTC) system"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2003 -> db", "Headquartered in Holland, Michigan -> db", "Provides electronic and mechanical design, software development -> /", "Offers double-sided SMT, flexible PCB, metal core PCB, through-hole, mixed technology assembly -> /", "Fine pitch placement to 01005, BGA -> /", "Conformal coating, IPC Class 2/3, PPAP capabilities -> /", "Automated selective wave soldering, microcontroller programming, 100% functional testing -> /", "Serves medical, industrial controls, durable goods, inspection lighting industries -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /quality", "Quality management system with PFMEA, PPAP, FAI, 8D, 5 Why, Fish Bone -> /quality", "On-site IPC training for employees -> /quality", "Track, Trace, and Control (TTC) system -> /quality", "First article approval process -> /quality", "Single source design and manufacturing -> /", "Component sourcing and supply chain management -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Westshore develops and manufactures electronic solutions for small and mid-tier manufacturers.", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='westshore-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Whaling City Solar was founded in 2020 in New Bedford, Massachusetts, to offer a better customer experience for residential and small-commercial solar purchases. The company was started by a team of engineers, project managers, and foremen who wanted to tailor each solar array to the specific home and owner, moving away from the high-pressure sales tactics common in the industry.

The firm handles the full installation process in-house, from initial site and financial assessment through permitting, installation, and commissioning. It manages all permitting paperwork—including Eversource interconnection agreements and town building and electrical permits—typically requiring two to five weeks for approvals. Installation crews usually complete a project in a single day, mounting rails and modules on the roof while simultaneously upgrading the electrical panel and inverters. The company works with equipment from brands such as REC, Solaria, and QCell modules; Enphase IQ8+ microinverters and SolarEdge string inverters; and Enphase Encharge, FranklinWH, and SPAN battery storage systems.

Whaling City Solar serves homeowners and small businesses across southeastern Massachusetts and Cape Cod, with recent projects completed in Mattapoisett, New Bedford, and Westport. Its service area covers the South Coast region, where the team lives and works, giving them familiarity with local weather, inspectors, and lenders.

