UPDATE companies SET description='Wil-Clair Sheet Metal was founded in 1999 in Kansas City, Missouri, by John Svetlecic after he left a previous sheet metal shop following a disagreement over company direction. He brought along two former employees, David Ogle to handle finances and Allen Kubicki to run the shop floor, both of whom remain with the company today.

It also provides engineering and drawing services to develop economical designs. The facility has expanded over the years to accommodate increased capacity, though specific square footage and annual part volumes are not disclosed.

Wil-Clair serves a diverse industrial base including food processing (Kellogg’s, Tyson), commercial signage (Procter & Gamble), plumbing and mechanical contracting (Stine-Nichols Plumbing), construction and entertainment (Worlds of Fun), and general industrial fabrication (CDI, Impact Fabrication). Customers range from large national brands to local design-build firms.

