UPDATE companies SET description='Wilkins Lumber Co. Inc. operates a sawmill in Milford, New Hampshire, a business the company traces to 1808. The mill has remained family-owned for more than two centuries, passing through generations while serving the Souhegan Valley and broader southern New Hampshire region. The current owners describe the operation as a small, family-run lumber mill.

The mill provides a log-to-lumber service that begins with selective harvesting for local timberland owners. It processes New Hampshire hemlock and pine, converting every scrap into competitively priced lumber products.

The company notes its history of supplying the Souhegan Valley continuously since the early 19th century, surviving the Great Depression, a fire, and a lightning strike in the first half of the 1900s.

