UPDATE companies SET description='Winkler Woods LLC was established in 2002 by Jorma Winkler, a fourth-generation wood industry expert, in Honolulu, Hawaii. Since 2003 the company has specialized in producing Koa and other exotic wood veneers and lumber, primarily for furniture making, with premium Koa veneers sourced from the slopes of Mauna Loa.

The company manufactures paper-backed (KamiPLY) and fleece-backed (WashiPLY) veneers from Hawaiian Koa, Mango, Monkey Pod, and Albizia, and supplies tonewood sets for soprano, concert, and tenor ukuleles as well as acoustic and electric guitars. Its hardwood lumber inventory includes figured curly Koa, spalted Mango, and Monkey Pod, available on a made-to-order basis. Winkler Woods operates a warehouse for online and wholesale sales, maintains distributors on the Big Island and Maui, and requires a minimum $1,500 purchase for tonewood sets.

Customers range from individual luthiers and guitar builders to furniture manufacturers and wholesale distributors worldwide. The firm serves both retail and wholesale markets, with tonewood sets matched for top, back, and sides, and veneers sold in standard and custom sizes.

Winkler Woods states its mission is to manufacture Hawaiian and exotic tonewoods, veneers, and lumber that showcase the beauty of creation, while its secondary mission emphasizes providing commercial benefit to landowners through a scientific and ecological approach to forest management. Core values cited are integrity, honesty, hard work, family, and efficiency.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Veneer production (paper-backed, fleece-backed)", "Tonewood set selection and matching", "Hardwood lumber sawmilling and sales", "Custom order fulfillment", "Wholesale distribution", "Consultancy services"], "industries": ["Musical instrument manufacturing", "Furniture manufacturing", "Wood veneer distribution", "Tonewood supply", "Forestry"], "materials": ["Hawaiian Koa", "Mango", "Monkey Pod", "Albizia", "Cuban Mahogany", "Ohia", "Kamani"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Koa veneers sourced from Mauna Loa", "Paper-backed (KamiPLY) and fleece-backed (WashiPLY) veneer options", "Extensive tonewood sets for ukulele (soprano, concert, tenor) and guitar (acoustic, electric)", "Wholesale distribution with local dealers on Big Island and Maui", "Minimum $1,500 order for tonewood sets"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2002 by Jorma Winkler -> page /", "Headquarters Honolulu, Hawaii -> db", "Produces Koa veneers (paper-backed KamiPLY, fleece-backed WashiPLY) -> page /", "Offers tonewood sets for ukuleles and guitars -> page /", "Minimum order $1,500 -> page /", "Materials: Hawaiian Koa, Mango, Monkey Pod, Albizia, Cuban Mahogany, Ohia, Kamani -> page /", "Wholesale distributors on Big Island and Maui -> page /", "Mission: manufacture Hawaiian and exotic tonewoods, veneers and lumber -> page /", "Core values: integrity, honesty, hard working, family, efficiency -> page /", "Secondary mission: commercial benefit to landowners with ecological approach -> page /", "Sourcing Koa from Mauna Loa -> page /", "Fourth-gen