UPDATE companies SET description='YellowLite was established in 2009 in Cleveland, Ohio, by former solar distribution executives who wanted to make solar energy more accessible to the masses. The company operates from its Cleveland headquarters with additional offices in Columbus and Cincinnati, serving customers across Ohio, Indiana, Michigan, and Pennsylvania.

The firm provides turnkey solar photovoltaic solutions, handling design, engineering, permitting, installation, and performance monitoring for residential, commercial, and agricultural projects. It also installs energy storage systems and offers repair and maintenance services. Since inception, YellowLite has completed over 4,000 solar installations across the Midwest.

Homeowners, businesses, and farms make up the core customer base. Agricultural projects often leverage USDA REAP grants, and the company supports energy storage for grid resilience.

