UPDATE companies SET description='Yoder Furniture Co. operates from two locations in central Kansas: its namesake store in Yoder and Country Home Furnishings in Pleasantview, five miles west of Hutchinson. The business traces its roots to March 1988, when Austin and Linda Miller opened Country Home Furnishings as a small storefront in Pleasantview. In the fall of 2002 they added the Yoder Furniture Co. location in Yoder, KS. The company remains family-owned and operated.

The retailer specializes in solid-wood furniture handcrafted by Amish and Mennonite builders across the Midwest. Rather than manufacturing, Yoder Furniture Co. hand-selects a network of independent shops to source a range of styles, wood species, and finishes. In addition to furniture, the stores carry home decor, quilts, gifts, table linens, coffee, candles, and canned goods such as jams and salsas.

By working directly with the builders, the company offers a broad selection of customizable options without acting as a producer itself.

That family-owned ethos and curated builder network remain the core of its value proposition.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Retail furniture sales", "Furniture sourcing from Amish and Mennonite builders", "Custom furniture options (styles, woods, finishes)"], "industries": ["Residential furniture retail", "Home furnishings retail"], "materials": ["Solid wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1988", "Direct relationships with Amish and Mennonite builders across the Midwest", "Curated network of hand-selected shops for wide style, wood, and finish selection", "Two physical showrooms in Yoder and Pleasantview, KS"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1988 by Austin and Linda Miller -> /about-us", "Family-owned and operated -> /about-us", "Two store locations: Yoder, KS and Pleasantview, KS -> /about-us, /", "Sources from Amish and Mennonite builders across Midwest -> /, /about-us", "Sells solid-wood furniture, decor, quilts, gifts, table linens, coffee, candles, canned goods -> /", "Employees contribute to success (no count) -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Retailer", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Selling handcrafted furniture since 1988, we offer solid-wood furniture from Amish and Mennonite builders across the Midwest. Be sure to visit our store locations, Yoder Furniture Co. in Yoder, KS or Country Home Furnishings, Pleasantview, KS", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='yoder-furniture-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='York Haven Fabricators (YHFAB) operates from York Haven, Pennsylvania. The company was established in 1998 by Henry Shefet as a division of Daisy Data, a ruggedized computer manufacturer he founded in 1982. The fabrication division expanded the business''s manufacturing knowledge into custom metal fabrication. In 2025, YHFAB became a subsidiary of S&W Metal Products, a Pennsylvania fabricator with roots dating to 1946.

YHFAB provides integrated sheet metal fabrication, heavy-gauge forming, welding, CNC machining, and finishing in a 160,000-square-foot facility. Processes include fiber laser cutting, CNC press brake and robotic bending, CNC turret punching, plate rolling, MIG/TIG/spot and robotic welding, surface finishing, and CNC milling (vertical, horizontal, 5-axis) and turning (multi-axis, live tooling). The shop runs 160-plus pieces of production equipment, employs 109-plus people, and ships more than 16,000 line items annually.

The company serves OEMs and manufacturers in energy (oil, gas, renewables), material handling, factory automation, automotive (OEM, Tier 1, Tier 2), commercial and industrial lighting, electronic enclosures, military, medical, and packaging sectors. It produces precision parts and assemblies for material handling systems, automation equipment, lighting fixtures, automotive components, and electronic housings.

YHFAB emphasizes a single-facility integration of fabrication and machining, backed by an ISO 9001:2015 quality system maintained since 2012. Inspection relies on a Virtek LaserQC system (±0.002 in) and a FARO Edge portable CMM (±0.0014 in). The firm also highlights its design-for-manufacture engineering and experience with custom factory automation systems.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser cutting", "CNC press brake forming", "Robotic bending", "CNC turret punching", "MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Spot welding", "Robotic welding", "Surface finishing", "Polishing", "Plate rolling", "Custom fabrication (prototype to high-volume)", "Design for manufacture", "CNC programming", "Solid modeling", "CNC milling (vertical, horizontal, 5-axis)", "CNC turning (multi-axis, live tooling)"], "industries": ["Energy", "Material Handling", "Factory Automation", "Automotive", "Lighting", "Electronics", "Military", "Medical", "Packaging"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Amada CNC turret punch", "Amada CNC press brake", "Amada flat laser", "Virtek LaserQC Inspection System", "FARO Edge Coordinate Measuring Machine", "Starrett Granite Slabs (48\u2033 x 72\u2033, 18\u2033 x 24\u2033)", "Mitutoyo calibrated height gauge (28\u2033)", "Fowler calibrated height gauge (24\u2033)"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.002 in (Virtek LaserQC), \u00b10.0014 in (FARO Edge CMM)", "built_on": ["Integrated fabrication and machining under one roof", "ISO 9001:2015 certified since 2012", "Advanced inspection with Virtek LaserQC and FARO Edge CMM", "Robotic welding cells for high-volume repeatability", "Design-for-manufacture engineering and CNC programming"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1998 by Henry Shefet as division of Daisy Data -> /about-us", "Acquired by S&W Metal Products in 2025 -> /about-us", "Headquarters York Haven, Pennsylvania -> db", "Facility size 160,000 sq ft -> /", "Employees 109+ -> /", "Production equipment 160+ -> /", "Annual line items shipped 16,000+ -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified since 2012 -> /quality", "Industries: energy, material handling, factory automation, automotive, lighting, electronics, military, medical, packaging -> /, /about-us", "Capabilities: laser cutting, CNC forming, turret punching, welding, robotic welding, finishing, rolling, CNC machining, engineering -> /capabilities", "Equipment: Amada CNC turret punch, press brake, flat laser; Virtek LaserQC; FARO Edge CMM; Starrett Granite Slabs; Mitutoyo/Fowler height gauges -> /about-us, /quality", "Tolerances: \u00b10.002 in (Virtek), \u00b10.0014 in (FARO) -> /quality", "Volume range: prototype to high-volume production runs -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "York Haven Fabricators, Inc. (YHFAB) is a state-of-the-art sheet metal fabricator and machining company.", "founded_year": "1998", "employee_count": "109+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='york-haven-fabricators' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='York Imperial Plastics, Inc. is a second-generation family-owned and operated plastic injection molding facility founded in 1985 in York, Pennsylvania. The company began as a custom molding operation and has since expanded into an all-inclusive service provider for tooling transfers, production molding, and value-added assembly.

The facility specializes in plastic injection molding from prototype through high-volume production, with a noted expertise in mold transfer and rework — over 500 successful transfers have been executed since 1985. Capabilities include multi-cavity high-production tool design, master unit die (MUD) systems, in-house assembly and packaging, and daily direct shipping of finished goods. Quality processes encompass APQP, PPAP, first-article inspection, CMM and optical measurement, color spectrophotometry, statistical process control, and moisture analysis.

York Imperial serves customers across a range of industries requiring custom plastic components, though specific sectors are not publicly listed. The company positions itself as a one-stop shop for manufacturers needing tooling construction, production molding, and logistics support under one roof.

